math> is :"}, "options": [{"id": "9d214c", "text": "<math><mn>240</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d92567dc"}, {"id": "3a4c31", "text": "<math><mn>82</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d92567dd"}, {"id": "0a62da", "text": "<math><mn>120</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d92567de"}, {"id": "a82ce3", "text": "<math><mn>164</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d92567df"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d92567e0", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfa3"], "topics": ["60e2fb3d66f9ce3f243b4d5e"], "concepts": ["60e2fb3c66f9ce3f243b4d30"], "question": {"text": "The number of triplets <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>z</mi></math>&nbsp;are distinct non negative integers satisfying <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>15</mn></math>, is"}, "options": [{"id": "d9df7c", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>80</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d92567e1"}, {"id": "9f3c76", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>136</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d92567e2"}, {"id": "88a70b", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>114</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d92567e3"}, {"id": "022c58", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>92</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d92567e4"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d92567e5", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfa3"], "topics": ["60c9e88bea0