1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn></math> and formed by using the digits <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math> only is:"}, "options": [{"id": "28d429", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>77</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d925680e"}, {"id": "b95997", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>82</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d925680f"}, {"id": "a62ded", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>42</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9256810"}, {"id": "bb1a77", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>35</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9256811"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9256812", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfa3"], "topics": ["60e2faac66f9ce3f243b4533"], "concepts": ["60e2fbbf66f9ce3f243b54a1"], "question": {"text": "A natural number has prime factorization given by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi></msup><msup><mn>3</mn><mi>y</mi></msup><msup><mn>5</mn><mi>z</mi></msup></math>, where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>z</mi></math> are such that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>6</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mi>z</mi></math>. Then the number of odd divisors of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math>, including <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math>, is:<gwmw style=\"display:none;\"></gwmw>"}, "options": [{"id": "aead1c", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>12</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9256813"}, {"id": "193122", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9256814"}, {"id": "791afc", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>11</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9256815"}, {"id": "d96ef4", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mi>x</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9256816"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9256817", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfa3"], "topics": ["60e2fb3d66f9ce3f243b4d5e"], "concepts": ["60e2fb3c66f9ce3f243b4d30"], "question": {"text": "The total number of positive integral solutions <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> such that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>24</mn></math> is :"}, "options": [{"id": "be2229", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>45</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9256818"}, {"id": "7bebdc", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>30</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9256819"}, {"id": "29d6e4", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>36</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d925681a"}, {"id": "4f1c3f", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>24</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d925681b"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d925681c", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfa3"], "topics": ["60e2fb7b66f9ce3f243b5123"], "concepts": ["60e2fb7a66f9ce3f243b5100"], "question": {"text": "Line $L_1$ of slope 2 and line $L_2$ of slope $\\frac{1}{2}$ intersect at the origin O . In the first quadrant, $\\mathrm{P}_1, \\mathrm{P}_2, \\ldots . \\mathrm{P}_{12}$ are 12 points on line $L_1$ and $Q_1, Q_2, \\ldots . . Q_9$ are 9 points on line $L_2$. Then the total number of triangles, that can be formed having vertices at three of the 22 points $\\mathrm{O}, \\mathrm{P}_1, \\mathrm{P}_2, \\ldots \\mathrm{P}_{12}$, $\\mathrm{Q}_1, \\mathrm{Q}_2, \\ldots . \\mathrm{Q}_9$, is:"}, "options": [{"id": "22af72", "text": "$1080$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d925681d"}, {"id": "5d2890", "text": "$1134$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d925681e"}, {"id": "24edb9", "text": "$1026$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d925681f"}, {"id": "c30706", "text": "$1188$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9256820"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9256821", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfa3"], "topics": ["60c9e88bea076dc381c0e100"], "concepts": ["6162fc2a6ed13040ec8576cb"], "question": {"text": "The number of ways, in which the letters $\\mathrm{A}, \\mathrm{B}, \\mathrm{C}$, D, E can be placed in the 8 boxes of the figure below so that no row remains empty and at most one letter can be placed in a box, is :<br/><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2Fjht4uFIEl7OzjP2g1vIqDgenIM5mxsHb7Sxpxed6htk.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\"/><br/>"}, "options": [{"id": "331567", "text": "$5880$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9256822"}, {"id": "8defa6", "text": "$960$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9256823"}, {"id": "205424", "text": "$840$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9256824"}, {"id": "cf4b5c", "text": "$5760$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9256825"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9256826", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfa3"], "topics": ["60e2faac66f9ce3f243b454b"], "concepts": ["60e2faab66f9ce3f243b4504"], "question": {"text": "Consider a class of <math><mn>5</mn></math> girls and <math><mn>7</mn></math> boys. The number of different teams consisting of <math><mn>2</mn></math> girls and <math><mn>3</mn></math> boys that can be formed from this class, if there are two specific boys <math><mi>A</mi></math> and <math><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo></math> who refuse to be the members of the same team, is:"}, "options": [{"id": "5fd325", "text": "<math><mn>300</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9256827"}, {"id": "1fb79d", "text": "<math><mn>200</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9256828"}, {"id": "4f63a1", "text": "<math><mn>500</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9256829"}, {"id": "9823d2", "text": "<math><mn>350</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d925682a"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d925682b", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfa3"], "topics": ["60e2fbc066f9ce3f243b54b7"], "concepts": ["60e5671b499d1e49588f87fb"], "question": {"text": "If the letters of the word MATHS are permuted and all possible words so formed are arranged as in a dictionary with serial numbers, then the serial number of the word THAMS is"}, "options": [{"id": "4b5a57", "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>103</mn></math></p>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d925682c"}, {"id": "57467d", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>102</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d925682d"}, {"id": "c0c155", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>101</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f