20</mn></math> questions of equal marks and the question paper is divided into three sections : <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>. A student is required to attempt total <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>15</mn></math> questions taking at least <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math> questions from each section. If section <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> has <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn></math> questions, section <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math> has <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn></math> questions and section <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> has <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn></math> questions, then the total number of ways a student can select <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>15</mn></math> questions is _________."}, "options": [{"id": "7b9cd7", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3c2ee0e063d9256871"}, {"id": "81da62", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3c2ee0e063d9256872"}, {"id": "1d8c58", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3c2ee0e063d9256873"}, {"id": "af50c1", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3c2ee0e063d9256874"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f3c2ee0e063d9256875", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfa3"], "topics": ["60e2faac66f9ce3f243b454b"], "concepts": ["60e2fb7a66f9ce3f243b50f6"], "question": {"text": "There are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn></math> students in class <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn></math> students in class <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>11</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn></math> students in class <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>12</mn><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;If the number of ways, in which <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn></math> students can be selected from them so as to include at least <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math> students from each class and at most <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn></math> students from the total <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>11</mn></math> students of class <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>11</mn></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>k</mi></math> is equal to"}, "options": [{"id": "a18e00", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3c2ee0e063d9256876"}, {"id": "bea6fa", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3c2ee0e063d9256877"}, {"id": "2ca3c9", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3c2ee0e063d9256878"}, {"id": "fcfe5b", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3c2ee0e063d9256879"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f3c2ee0e063d925687a", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfa3"], "topics": ["60e2faac66f9ce3f243b4533"], "concepts": ["60e2fbc066f9ce3f243b54ae"], "question": {"text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"}\" open=\"{\"><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"}\" open=\"{\"><mrow><mn>9</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>11</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mo>,</mo><mn>1000</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>. If<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"}\" open=\"{\"><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>:</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;then the sum of all the elements in the set <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>A</mi></math>&nbsp;is equal to _______."}, "options": [{"id": "d00b7d", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3c2ee0e063d925687b"}, {"id": "1013f7", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3c2ee0e063d925687c"}, {"id": "904cb1", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3c2ee0e063d925687d"}, {"id": "114d48", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3c2ee0e063d925687e"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f3c2ee0e063d925687f", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfa3"], "topics": ["60e2fb3d66f9ce3f243b4d5e"], "concepts": ["60e2fb3c66f9ce3f243b4d30"], "question": {"text": "The total number of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo></math>digit numbers whose sum of digits is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn></math>, is .........."}, "options": [{"id": "092f55", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3c2ee0e063d9256880"}, {"id": "763727", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3c2ee0e063d9256881"}, {"id": "40e535", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3c2ee0e063d9256882"}, {"id": "0312eb", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3c2ee0e063d9256883"}], "questionLabels": []}], "markingSche